[Case Study 1: RAG System & HR/ATS Agent]
1. The Problem
Studying and extracting information from massive document sets takes too much manual effort and time. I needed a personal RAG system where I could upload lectures or documents and get precise summaries and answers driven purely by the provided context, without hallucinations.

2. What I Did & Decided
Architecture: Built a full backend architecture using FastAPI.

Chunking Strategy: Configured a chunk size of 500 with an overlap of 100 to maintain semantic context across boundaries and avoid data loss during retrieval.

Embeddings & Vector Store: Used Sentence Transformers for vector embeddings, storing vectors, metadata, and text chunks in ChromaDB.

LLM Engine: Integrated Groq API during testing for fast latency, structured to switch seamlessly to OpenAI or Gemini endpoints.

Agentic Design: Designed it as an Agentic workflow equipped with custom tools, allowing the engine to adapt to broader document tasks rather than simple semantic search.

3. What Came of It
The system drastically reduced the time needed to parse through lecture files. Beyond study workflows, its agentic architecture made it fully adaptable for HR/ATS workflows—taking candidate resumes, querying skills, and evaluating candidates against specific job requirements with exact contextual precision.

